344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 134 0 R/T(1. INTRODUCTION)/E(1. INTRODUCTION)/Pg 20 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

345 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 134 0 R/E(Large quantities of food, clothing, electronic devices, educational materials, and household resources are wasted even though many people and organizations require these resources. Restaurants, hotels, educational institutions, households, and businesses may have surplus resources that could help others. However, without an organized platform, it is often difficult to identify genuine recipients and distribute available resources efficiently.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

346 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 134 0 R/E(Traditional donation systems generally depend on manual searching, personal contacts, or social media communication. These approaches may not efficiently identify suitable recipients based on their actual needs. In addition, donors may not have sufficient information about the quantity, urgency, location, and condition of the resources required by receivers.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

347 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 134 0 R/E(To address these challenges, this project proposes Smart Donation Connect, an AI-enabled platform that connects donors with verified receivers. The system uses intelligent matching techniques to consider resource type, quantity, condition, urgency, and geographical location. In addition, the platform can analyze historical food-related information to predict future demand and identify possible surplus resources.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

348 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 134 0 R/E(The proposed system aims to reduce resource wastage while improving the efficiency and reliability of the donation process. It provides a structured platform through which donors can list available resources and receivers can post their requirements. The system then assists in identifying suitable donor\205receiver pairs and tracks the donation process until completion.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

349 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 135 0 R/T(1.1 OVERVIEW OF THE PROJECT)/E(1.1 OVERVIEW OF THE PROJECT)/Pg 21 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

350 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E(Smart Donation Connect is an AI-enabled web application designed to reduce resource wastage and connect donors with people and organizations in need. Large quantities of food, clothing, electronic devices, educational materials, and other reusable items are often wasted by hotels, restaurants, businesses, and households. At the same time, NGOs, orphanages, old-age homes, educational institutions, and economically disadvantaged communities face shortages of essential resources.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

351 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E(The proposed system provides a common platform where donors can register and list available resources, while beneficiaries can register and post their requirements. A verification process helps improve the reliability of donor and beneficiary profiles. The system uses intelligent donor\205receiver matching to identify suitable recipients based on donation type, quantity, urgency, availability, and geographical location.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

352 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E(An important feature of the project is the AI-based food demand prediction model. It analyzes historical sales data, seasonal trends, festivals, weather conditions, and customer patterns to estimate food demand and identify potential surplus food. This information can help restaurants and hotels plan food preparation and reduce unnecessary waste.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

353 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E( )/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

354 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E(The platform also provides real-time notifications and donation tracking to support the donation process. Donations are tracked through different stages, including posting, matching, acceptance, collection, delivery, and completion. These features help users monitor the progress of donations and improve coordination between donors and beneficiaries.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

355 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 135 0 R/T(1.2. OBJECTIVE)/E(1.2. OBJECTIVE)/Pg 21 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 135 0 R/E(The main objective of Smart Donation Connect is to reduce resource wastage, improve donation efficiency, and ensure that available resources reach genuine beneficiaries. By combining artificial intelligence, location-based matching, user verification, and donation tracking, the proposed system aims to encourage charitable participation and support social welfare and sustainable development.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

357 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 136 0 R/T(2. LITERATURE REVIEW)/E(2. LITERATURE REVIEW)/Pg 22 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

358 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 136 0 R/E(2.1 Literature Overview)/Pg 22 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 136 0 R/E(The literature review examines existing approaches related to food waste reduction, food demand prediction, online donation systems, and resource sharing. These approaches demonstrate how artificial intelligence, machine learning, and digital platforms can help reduce resource wastage and improve the distribution of essential items to people in need.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 136 0 R/E(Machine-learning-based food demand forecasting helps estimate future food requirements by analyzing historical data and relevant patterns. This can support hotels and restaurants in planning food preparation and identifying possible surplus food. Digital food-sharing and online donation platforms provide methods for connecting people who have extra resources with individuals or organizations that require assistance.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

361 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 136 0 R/E(Location-based resource-sharing systems can help identify nearby recipients and)/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
