<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 137 0 R/T(This study examines the use of food-sharing platforms by hospitality and food-service businesses. Hotels and restaurants may have surplus food that could be distributed to people in need instead of being wasted. Digital platforms can support the sharing process by connecting available food with potential recipients. Smart Donation Connect builds on this concept by including location-based matching, user verification, notifications, and donation tracking.)/E(This study examines the use of food-sharing platforms by hospitality and food-service businesses. Hotels and restaurants may have surplus food that could be distributed to people in need instead of being wasted. Digital platforms can support the sharing process by connecting available food with potential recipients. Smart Donation Connect builds on this concept by including location-based matching, user verification, notifications, and donation tracking.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[1]>>
